'''''Eruca''''' is a genus of [[flowering plant]]s in the family [[Brassicaceae]], native to the [[Mediterranean region]], western and Central Asia, and China.<ref name = powo/> It includes the leaf vegetable known as [[Eruca sativa|rocket or arugula]].

==Description==
The species can be either [[annual plant|annual]] or [[biennial plant|biennial]], growing to 20–100&nbsp;cm tall. The [[leaf|leaves]] are deeply pinnately lobed with four to ten small lateral lobes and a large terminal lobe. The [[flower]]s are 2–4&nbsp;cm diameter, arranged in a [[Inflorescence#Simple inflorescences|corymb]], with the typical 4-petal, 4-sepal [[Brassicaceae]] flower structure; the petals are creamy white with purple veins, and the stamens yellow. The [[fruit]] is a [[Siliqua (plant)|siliqua]] (pod) 12–25&nbsp;mm long with an apical beak, and containing several [[seed]]s.<ref name=blamey>Blamey, M. & Grey-Wilson, C. (1989). ''Flora of Britain and Northern Europe''. {{ISBN|0-340-40170-2}}</ref><ref name=fnwe>Flora of NW Europe: [http://ip30.eti.uva.nl/BIS/flora.php?selected=beschrijving&menuentry=soorten&id=2395 ''Eruca vesicaria''] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20071014021510/http://ip30.eti.uva.nl/BIS/flora.php?selected=beschrijving&menuentry=soorten&id=2395 |date=2007-10-14 }}</ref><ref name=rhs>Huxley, A., ed. (1992). ''New RHS Dictionary of Gardening''. Macmillan {{ISBN|0-333-47494-5}}.</ref>

==Species==
The number of species is disputed, with some authorities only accepting a single species, while others accept up to six species.<ref name=mc>Med-Checklist: [http://ww2.bgbm.org/mcl/PTaxonDetail.asp?NameId=23926&PTRefFK=1275 ''Eruca'']</ref><ref name=mc1>Med-Checklist: [http://ww2.bgbm.org/mcl/PTaxonDetail.asp?NameId=23930&PTRefFk=1275 ''Eruca vesicaria'' aggregate]</ref> ''[[Plants of the World Online]]'' accepts six species:<ref name = powo/>
*''[[Eruca aurea]]'' {{small|Batt.}}
*''[[Eruca foleyi]]'' {{small|(Batt.) Lorite, Perfectti, J.M.Gómez, Gonz.-Megías & Abdelaziz}}
*''[[Eruca longirostris]]'' {{small|Uechtr.}}
*''[[Eruca pinnatifida]]'' {{small|(Desf.) Pomel}} (syn. ''E. sativa'' subsp. ''pinnatifida'' {{small|(Desf.) Batt.}}; ''E. vesicaria'' subsp. ''pinnatifida'' {{small|(Desf.) Emberger & Maire}})
*''[[Eruca sativa]]'' {{small|Mill.}} (syn. ''E. vesicaria'' subsp. ''sativa'' {{small|(Mill.) Thell.}})
*''[[Eruca vesicaria]]'' {{small|(L.) Cav.}}

When treated as a monospecific genus, all are included within ''E. vesicaria''.<ref name=foc>Flora of China: [http://www.efloras.org/florataxon.aspx?flora_id=2&taxon_id=112128 ''Eruca'']</ref><ref name=fe>Flora Europaea: [http://rbg-web2.rbge.org.uk/cgi-bin/nph-readbtree.pl/feout?FAMILY_XREF=&GENUS_XREF=Eruca&SPECIES_XREF=&TAXON_NAME_XREF=&RANK= ''Eruca'']</ref>

